cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "RL-Trader: Generalization and Evaluation Rigor in Deep Reinforcement Learning"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch study of two deep-RL failure modes — trajectory memorization and
  single-seed unreliability — using financial markets as a hard, non-stationary
  testbed. Implements PPO, two Gymnasium market environments, and an evaluation
  suite (domain-randomization ablation, multi-seed significance testing, and a
  surrogate-data falsification test) that finds no seed-robust market edge, in line
  with weak-form efficiency, and reproduces Henderson et al. (2018) in a new domain.
type: software
